  "topography": {
    "project_purpose": "Altitude.Fi is an Ethereum DeFi borrowing and lending aggregator focused on self-repaying loans against BTC and ETH collateral. The protocol routes collateral and debt positions through integrations such as Aave, Morpho, and other venues to optimize rates, uses vault-based accounting with supply and debt tokens, and applies yield/rebalancing mechanics to help pay down USDC debt over time.",
    "relationship_narrative": "All product families share the core Altitude.Fi contracts (VaultERC20, SupplyToken, DebtToken) as their implementation logic. The v2 pools (cbBTC-USDC and wstETH-USDC) reuse the same FarmBufferDispatcher and VaultRegistryV1 infrastructure, while the v1 wstETH-USDC pool appears to be an earlier, less modular version.",
